-- title:
--   Finiteness of the residue field of the local Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$, a set $S$ of natural numbers, and a ring $\mathcal{O}$ which is a commutative domain, a discrete valuation ring, and complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of cusp forms of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Assume, as a `Fact`, that [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6) holds, i.e. that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule spanned by the cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space, and assume that the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ is finite. The conclusion is that the residue field of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) is finite, where the latter ring is the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` at the submonoid obtained by applying `latticeBaseChange N S 𝒪` to the complement of the prime ideal `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ`.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement for the residual field of the local Hecke algebra attached to a mod-$\mathfrak{m}$ Hecke eigensystem $\theta$ with values in the residue field of a complete discrete valuation ring; it records that passing from $\mathcal{O}$ to the local Hecke algebra does not enlarge the residue field beyond finiteness. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_heckeCoefficientRing_of_hasIntegralStructure`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_heckeCoefficientRing_of_hasIntegralStructure), where a coefficient ring with finite residue field is produced. The statement asserts finiteness only; no bound on the cardinality of the residue field is given, and nothing is asserted when the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ is infinite.
